From 744de0e43aaea0b061735acaba50211e6594d437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:10:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 065/101] script: the layer transform API, createLayer and
 destroyLayer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SceneScript's ILayer.getTransformMatrix was missing: 5 of the library's scenes (3243449890, 3319542538,
3326873240, 3516106265, 3516174947) call it in init to pick a side of the screen, and the shared values
their other scripts read never got set (7 more errors of "cannot read property 'x' of undefined").
thisScene.createLayer returned undefined: 2469881470, 2828233985 and 2890767643 build their visualiser
bars with it (64 bars from one), and WE's own clock preset builds its text shadow with it.

- ILayer: getTransformMatrix (the world matrix with the parents', scene units, y up, as `origin`),
  rotateObjectSpace, lookAt / lookAtYaw (the layer's -z towards the target), setParent (with
  adjustTransforms, a puppet attachment, a cycle refused), getAttachmentIndex / Matrix / Origin / Angles
  (a puppet's attachments, posed), in JS over four natives with WE's own Mat4. getParent is undefined
  when unparented, as WE's docs say (it was null).
- IImageLayer.alignment reads and writes (the quad is placed from it next frame); ITextLayer font,
  anchor, padding, limitrows, limitwidth, opaquebackground read.
- IScene.createLayer: an asset path (models/ → image, particles/ → particle, a sound, an .mdl), an
  IAssetHandle, or a layer's configuration as scene.json writes it (serialised with WE's
  _Internal.stringifyConfig, so vectors are "x y z"), built now with a new id, last in the layer list
  and drawn last before the bloom. destroyLayer takes a layer out of the lists (freed with the scene);
  engine.isObjectValid is false for it. getLayerByID.
- The draw loop walks a copy of the draw order: a text layer's script runs while it renders and may
  create, destroy or sort layers.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md (SceneScript coverage); docs/player/reports/scene-health.md
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
